256
00:16:40,210 --> 00:16:43,050
Hooray, Tsubasa-senpai!

257
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:46,050
I have to tell his father.

258
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:58,770
I see, they advanced to the semifinals.

259
00:17:00,230 --> 00:17:02,440
Good luck, Tsubasa.

260
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:12,120
Where's Tsubasa-kun?

261
00:17:13,330 --> 00:17:16,580
We won today, I'm sure he's reporting to the manager Sanae.

262
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:17,750
You're right.

263
00:17:17,830 --> 00:17:21,000
Tsubasa-kun, score a goal in my heart too.

264
00:17:21,090 --> 00:17:22,840
You don't sound anything like her.

265
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:30,970
Yes, we managed to win through the kids' cooperation.

266
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:34,970
Congratulations on advancing to the final.

267
00:17:35,310 --> 00:17:40,400
Our next match is against France, they are a strong team, we have to focus a lot.

268
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:46,650
We will all support you from here, as loudly as those in Paris.

269
00:17:47,570 --> 00:17:48,740
Very well.

270
00:17:56,330 --> 00:17:57,250
- Hey...
- Hey...

271
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:03,500
What happened?

272
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:06,880
Yes, well, I...

273
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:09,130
Oh, so you're here.

274
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:11,390
Abola, Sanae.

275
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,140
Ishizaki-kun?

276
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:18,520
Oh, I hope you saw that block with my face that helped our victory.

277
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,230
Tsubasa did a great job leading the team.

278
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:24,770
I bet you fell in love with him again.

279
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:27,860
I think you really found a wonderful husband.

280
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,530
Ah-Ishizaki-kun.

281
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:32,910
If you come here to support us, I'm sure Tsubasa...

282
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,870
Woooow, shut up!

283
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:35,790
Nakazawa Sanae - Call ended.

284
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:37,580
She hung up.

285
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:40,330
She got embarrassed.

286
00:18:42,130 --> 00:18:43,630
Monkey!

287
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:48,340
Aaaaaaa! Aaaaaaa!

288
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:50,880
I'm sorry, I think I disturbed you.

289
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:52,180
It's fine.

290
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,470
Tsubasa-kun.

291
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,260
Can you come for a minute?

292
00:18:57,390 --> 00:19:01,600
What? You haven't spoken with Tsubasa-kun at all?

293
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:06,360
No, but it's okay. I want him to focus on the France match.

294
00:19:06,690 --> 00:19:10,610
I see. Long-distance relationships are hard.

295
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:13,240
Ohhh, don't annoy me.

296
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,870
Oh, speaking of which...

297
00:19:15,370 --> 00:19:21,120
Yayoi-chan seems very happy because she received a nice postcard from Misugi-kun.

298
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:22,870
Look, here it is.

299
00:19:23,210 --> 00:19:25,080
Oh, it's very beautiful.

300
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:31,800
That kid.

301
00:19:31,970 --> 00:19:33,550
Pardon.

302
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:40,140
Catch.

303
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,890
Thanks.

304
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,230
Did something happen?

305
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,780
Huh? No, nothing happened.

306
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:59,160
What? The São Paulo youth team?

307
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:04,710
Yes, they had a friendly match in Paris.

308
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:08,420
And their coach is Roberto Hongo.

309
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:15,220
I see. So Roberto has become a youth team coach in Brazil.

310
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,430
Tsubasa!

311
00:20:17,510 --> 00:20:19,060
What is it, Roberto?

312
00:20:19,390 --> 00:20:22,640
Remember, the ball is your friend.

313
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:27,560
Well done, Tsubasa!

314
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:36,530
You're amazing, Tsubasa.

315
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:43,830
This team is at the top in Brazil and hasn't lost any match in Paris.

316
00:20:45,370 --> 00:20:50,840
Thanks, Misaki-kun. Even though you're tired from the match, you went and researched it.

317
00:20:51,170 --> 00:20:53,550
No, it's not a big deal.

318
00:20:53,630 --> 00:20:58,760
And also, their team played their last match

319
00:20:58,930 --> 00:21:01,760
near the stadium on the day we advanced to the semifinals.

320
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:05,100
The match started at 9:30.

321
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:09,400
Then they returned to Brazil in the afternoon.

322
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:12,400
I see, so they returned to Brazil.

323
00:21:15,610 --> 00:21:17,360
What do you want to do, Tsubasa?

324
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:26,460
I want to see you, Roberto.

325
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:54,530
He's here.

326
00:21:54,610 --> 00:21:55,440
Yes.

327
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,700
Welcome.

328
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:02,700
A strong player is added to the German youth.

329
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:06,910
The legendary goalkeeper, Dieter Müller-kun.